lezni)<\/em><\/p><p>The magician performed a quick _______ of the eye, making the coin disappear. <em>(kacsint\u00e1s \/ tr\u00fckk)<\/em><\/p><p>Don&#039;t take everything he says so seriously; he&#039;s often just _______. <em>(viccel \/ po\u00e9nkodik)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">kacsint\u00e1s \/ biccent\u00e9s \/ jelz\u00e9s \/ mosoly \/ szemrebben\u00e9s<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): komolyan v\u00e9tel \/ szigor\u00fa tekintet \/ figyelmen k\u00edv\u00fcl hagy\u00e1s<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ at someone = kacsintani valakire (pl. He winked at me from across the bar.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 a knowing _______ = tud\u00f3, titkos kacsint\u00e1s (pl. She gave him a knowing wink.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ and _______ = kacsintani \u00e9s mosolyogni (gyakran viccel\u0151dve) (pl. He winked and grinned.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ a secret = titokban kacsintani (pl. They winked a secret message to each other.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p>noun: <strong>wink<\/strong><\/p><p>verb: <strong>wink<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: wink and smile \/ wink at \/ a wink of \/ wink of an eye<\/span><\/p><p>similar: blink \/ signal \/ nod \/ gesture<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: stare \/ frown \/ glare<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":null,"study_direction":"front_to_back","color":"#64f2da","review":{"state":"review","interval":3,"lapses":1,"is_leech":false},"previews":{"again":"1 perc (\u2192 1 nap)","hard":"4 nap","good":"7 nap","easy":"9 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-05-12T20:39:48+00:00"},{"id":49586,"front":"<p>The new car&#039;s paint job had a beautiful _______ that reflected the sunlight. <em>(f\u00e9nyess\u00e9g \/ csillog\u00e1s)<\/em><\/p><p>The politician&#039;s speech was full of empty _______, offering no real solutions. <em>(sz\u00f3lam \/ \u00fcres besz\u00e9d)<\/em><\/p><p>The academic paper provided a detailed _______ of the historical event, exploring various interpretations. <em>(magyar\u00e1zat \/ \u00e9rtelmez\u00e9s)<\/em><\/p><p>She ran a _______ over the difficult passage in the book, trying to understand its deeper meaning. <em>(\u00e1tfut \/ gyorsan elolvas)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">f\u00e9nyess\u00e9g \/ csillog\u00e1s \/ magyar\u00e1zat \/ \u00e9rtelmez\u00e9s \/ sz\u00f3lam<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): matt \/ hom\u00e1lyos \/ \u00e9rthetetlen<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 a high _______ = magas f\u00e9nyess\u00e9g (pl. The table had a high _______ that made it look very modern.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 run a _______ over = \u00e1tfutni, gyorsan elolvasni (pl. I&#039;ll just run a _______ over the report before the meeting.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ on something = magyar\u00e1zat, komment\u00e1r valamihez (pl. The professor offered some helpful _______ on the complex theory.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 empty _______ = \u00fcres besz\u00e9d, semmitmond\u00f3 sz\u00f3lam (pl. His promises turned out to be just empty _______.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p>noun: <strong>gloss<\/strong><\/p><p>verb: <strong>gloss<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: high gloss \/ gloss over \/ glossary of terms \/ glossy finish<\/span><\/p><p>similar: sheen \/ lustre \/ shine \/ explanation<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: matte \/ dull \/ obscure<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":null,"study_direction":"back_to_front","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"review","interval":3,"lapses":0,"is_leech":false},"previews":{"again":"1 perc (\u2192 1 nap)","hard":"4 nap","good":"7 nap","easy":"9 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-05-14T21:05:08+00:00"},{"id":51177,"fr